C. first-order (v/c)^2 coefficients
  J=0: massive coeff = 0 (J(J+1)/4 = 0),  massless coeff = 0 (J^2/2 = 0)
  J=1: massive coeff = 1/2 (J(J+1)/4 = 1/2),  massless coeff = 1/2 (J^2/2 = 1/2)
  J=2: massive coeff = 3/2 (J(J+1)/4 = 3/2),  massless coeff = 2 (J^2/2 = 2)
  J=3: massive coeff = 3 (J(J+1)/4 = 3),  massless coeff = 9/2 (J^2/2 = 9/2)
  J=4: massive coeff = 5 (J(J+1)/4 = 5),  massless coeff = 8 (J^2/2 = 8)
  J=5: massive coeff = 15/2 (J(J+1)/4 = 15/2),  massless coeff = 25/2 (J^2/2 = 25/2)
  J=6: massive coeff = 21/2 (J(J+1)/4 = 21/2),  massless coeff = 18 (J^2/2 = 18)
  J=7: massive coeff = 14 (J(J+1)/4 = 14),  massless coeff = 49/2 (J^2/2 = 49/2)
  J=8: massive coeff = 18 (J(J+1)/4 = 18),  massless coeff = 32 (J^2/2 = 32)
  from the ODEs at x=1: P_J'(1) = J(J+1)/2 (Legendre: -2y' + J(J+1)y = 0), T_J'(1) = J^2 (Chebyshev: -y' + J^2 y = 0)

D. spin needed for an O(1) change at v = 120 km/s
  (v/c)^2 = 1.602216e-07;  J(J+1)/4 (v/c)^2 = 1 -> J = 4996.0;  J^2/2 (v/c)^2 = 1 -> J = 3533.1
  J=    2: P_J(gamma*)-1 = 2.40332e-7,  T_J(gamma*)-1 = 3.20443e-7
  J=   10: P_J(gamma*)-1 = 4.4061e-6,  T_J(gamma*)-1 = 8.01109e-6
  J=  100: P_J(gamma*)-1 = 0.000404601,  T_J(gamma*)-1 = 0.000801215
  J= 3533: P_J(gamma*)-1 = 0.566231,  T_J(gamma*)-1 = 1.17812
  J= 4996: P_J(gamma*)-1 = 1.27956,  T_J(gamma*)-1 = 2.76141
  (single-spin residues increase with v; none decreases -> no single exchange is a gate)

